<title>FINLAND: M-Serla says deals to help 1998 earnings.</title>
<headline>M-Serla says deals to help 1998 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish forestry group Metsa-Serla Oy said on Tuesday its recent acquisitions would slightly depress its 1997 earnings, but have a positive impact on 1998 earnings.</p>
<p>&quot;These (deals) including restructuring costs will slightly depress 1997 earnings...but they will have a significantly bigger positive impact on 1998 earnings,&quot; Metsa-Serla finance director Ari Martonen told a news conference after the company said it would buy part of Swiss firm Biber Holding AG.</p>
<p>Last week it agreed to buy mills from its Finnish rival UPM-Kymmene Oy.</p>
</text>
